{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01VVSSEAPL5yRoHHrUe33hHP", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://booklive.jp/product/index/title_id/40000492/vol_no/001\"}, {\"url\": \"https://aisf.or.jp/%7Ejaanus/deta/o/oomon.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://projects.mcah.columbia.edu/jaanus/node/2113\"}, {\"url\": \"https://book.douban.com/series/36920?page=3\"}, {\"url\": \"https://aisf.or.jp/%7Ejaanus/deta/o/oodoguchi.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://aisf.or.jp/~jaanus/deta/n/naijimon.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/shigaku/117/8/117_KJ00005018716/_article/-char/ja\"}, {\"url\": \"https://projects.mcah.columbia.edu/jaanus/node/1897\"}, {\"url\": \"https://muse.jhu.edu/article/679244/figure/fig05\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T22:58:29.819Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "清俗紀聞 「大門の内、少し間を置いてまた扉を設く」", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01MtZGa6YTRw3dVwAtojuFpc", "content": [{"title": "booklive.jp", "url": "https://booklive.jp/product/index/title_id/40000492/vol_no/001"}, {"title": "aisf.or.jp", "url": "https://aisf.or.jp/%7Ejaanus/deta/o/oomon.htm"}, {"title": "nezumikido 鼠木戸", "url": "https://projects.mcah.columbia.edu/jaanus/node/2113"}, {"title": "book.douban.com", "url": "https://book.douban.com/series/36920?page=3"}, {"title": "aisf.or.jp", "url": "https://aisf.or.jp/%7Ejaanus/deta/o/oodoguchi.htm"}, {"title": "aisf.or.jp", "url": "https://aisf.or.jp/~jaanus/deta/n/naijimon.htm"}, {"title": "www.jstage.jst.go.jp", "url": "https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/shigaku/117/8/117_KJ00005018716/_article/-char/ja"}, {"title": "ōdoguchi 大戸口", "url": "https://projects.mcah.columbia.edu/jaanus/node/1897"}, {"title": "Meisho zue and the Mapping of Prosperity in Late Tokugawa Japan", "url": "https://muse.jhu.edu/article/679244/figure/fig05"}]}, "The search didn't find the exact passage 「大門の内、少し間を置いてまた扉を設く」 in any result, so I couldn't confirm the original wording or its context in the book.\n\nWhat the results do cover:\n\n- **The book:** A Tōyō Bunko edition from Heibonsha describes a record compiled by Nakagawa Tadahide, the Nagasaki magistrate, from interviews in the 1790s with Qing merchants from Fujian, Zhejiang, and Jiangsu, covering their institutions, customs, objects, and religion. The first volume covers annual events, household life, and clothing. The digital edition is on BookLive, and the publisher's catalogue lists Murematsu Kazuya as the editor and commentator.\n- **Related architecture terms:** Japanese architecture references describe a 大門 (ōmon) as a large gate that functions as the entrance to a nobleman's mansion or a castle. Separately, the 大戸口 (ōdoguchi) is the main entrance of a traditional house, which was closed with an ōdo (great door), the size and solidity of which were believed to have given the entrance its name. These are Japanese house and gate terms, not Qing-specific descriptions, so they may not match the passage you're asking about.\n\nTo find the passage, try searching for the Tōyō Bunko text itself, a digitized copy from the National Diet Library, or Chinese-language scholarship on the 《清俗紀聞》 gate and door descriptions."], "durationSeconds": 6.1386976660000006, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01VVSSEAPL5yRoHHrUe33hHP", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
